preConditionHook:
// EL: minlist(open, close) and maxlist(open, close) -- the body's bottom and
// top, whichever way the bar closed. They select among raw open and close,
// tick-grid price operands and exactly the scope their ACCEPTED row allows, so
// plain comparisons stand in for them. Scratch locals, reset every bar, and
// declared locals rather than hook-scope doubles so a second placement of the
// rule gets its own prefixed copy.
//
// The rule itself: after a bear trend bar, this bar's body shrinks to at most
// bodyShrink of that prior body AND it shows a lower tail of at least
// tailFraction of its own range -- exhaustion, read as a countertrend long.
// Mirrored after a bull bar. The prior body is read DIRECTLY rather than
// against a window average, which is what the shrink ratio already measures,
// so the rule needs no window at all.
bodyTop = open[0];
if (close[0] > bodyTop) bodyTop = close[0];
bodyBottom = open[0];
if (close[0] < bodyBottom) bodyBottom = close[0];
